WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.679
Now that we have the game mode created,

2
00:00:04.679 --> 00:00:08.800
let's go ahead and talk about Blueprint interfaces.

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.880
Now, Blueprint interfaces are a special way

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.279
that you can very cheaply send information

5
00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:19.199
to and from various actors inside of Unreal Engine 5.

6
00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:23.600
We create our interfaces by right-clicking inside

7
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.120
of the content browser, going to Blueprints,

8
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.879
and then selecting a Blueprint interface.

9
00:00:28.879 --> 00:00:31.359
When we create this Blueprint interface,

10
00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:35.359
you're going to notice that the graph is similar but slightly

11
00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:36.560
different.

12
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.039
That's because with these Blueprint interfaces,

13
00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.479
we are defining a method of communication.

14
00:00:43.479 --> 00:00:45.880
So what we're doing is we're basically

15
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.960
defining the objects or the inputs and outputs

16
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.560
that we want this interface to interact with.

17
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.600
And then instead of having to cast to multiple Blueprints

18
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.759
or load up multiple Blueprints just

19
00:00:58.759 --> 00:01:00.920
to work with this information, we

20
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.000
can just make sure that it has this interface.

21
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.640
So what we're going to do now is we're

22
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.480
going to go into the editor, and we're

23
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.719
going to make an interface.

24
00:01:07.719 --> 00:01:10.040
And then in our interface, what we're going to do

25
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.159
is we're going to add two integer inputs called

26
00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:14.760
score and time.

27
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.840
So let's pop over to the editor, and let's do that now.

28
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.799
So I'm going to hit Control-Space,

29
00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:22.560
and for some reason, there we go, that is pulling up now.

30
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.599
And I'm going to come up here to my content folder.

31
00:01:24.599 --> 00:01:26.319
I'm just going to do this at the root of it,

32
00:01:26.359 --> 00:01:27.480
and I'm going to right-click.

33
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.120
We're going to go Blueprints, and we're

34
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.280
going to go Blueprint Interface.

35
00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.680
Now, I like to label these for BPI, or Blueprint Interface,

36
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.989
and we're going to call this one.

37
00:01:41.989 --> 00:01:44.269
And let's double-click on it to open it up.

38
00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:47.030
And again, there is going to be no way for us

39
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.989
to draw or drag off of this.

40
00:01:48.989 --> 00:01:52.750
We do have the ability to name our function here.

41
00:01:52.750 --> 00:02:03.409
So we're going to go ahead and call this pickUpObject.

42
00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:05.530
And then what we're going to do is

43
00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.010
we're going to come to our inputs,

44
00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:08.810
and we're going to add 1 and 2.

45
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:15.419
And so we're going to call one of them score,

46
00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:17.979
and we're going to call the other one time.

47
00:02:17.979 --> 00:02:19.740
And we also need to make sure that we

48
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.419
set these to be integers, because our score and our time

49
00:02:24.419 --> 00:02:25.860
are going to be integer values.

50
00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.270
And it looked like I took my time there,

51
00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:29.949
so there we go.

52
00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.550
So let's go ahead and compile and save.

53
00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.509
Now, once we have our interface created,

54
00:02:35.509 --> 00:02:39.270
we need to let whatever we want to interact with

55
00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.949
know about where that interface is.

56
00:02:40.949 --> 00:02:42.229
And to do this, what we're going to do

57
00:02:42.229 --> 00:02:44.349
is we're going to locate our advanced vehicle

58
00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:46.750
pawn, because that is the pawn that we're

59
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.990
going to be controlling.

60
00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.189
We're going to open it up, and we're

61
00:02:49.189 --> 00:02:50.870
going to go to its class settings.

62
00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.710
And then inside of its class settings,

63
00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:56.509
there is this option called Implemented Interfaces.

64
00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.550
We are going to implement this interface.

65
00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.509
So let's pop back over to the editor now.

66
00:03:02.509 --> 00:03:04.030
And I can go ahead and close this.

67
00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.629
Let me just make sure that I've saved it.

68
00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:05.990
Great.

69
00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:06.909
We're going to close this.

70
00:03:06.909 --> 00:03:08.870
And I'm going to hit Control-Space again

71
00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.110
to bring up my content browser, which there we go.

72
00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.270
We're going to our vehicle template, our Blueprint.

73
00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.669
And then we're going to look for our vehicle advanced pawn,

74
00:03:16.669 --> 00:03:19.370
and I'm going to double-click on that to open it up.

75
00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:22.090
Then inside of our class settings,

76
00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.449
we're going to go over here to our Implemented.

77
00:03:24.449 --> 00:03:26.210
Then we're going to click on this Add.

78
00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.610
And if we just search for VPI, here we go.

79
00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.330
There's our VPI stats.

80
00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.770
And we've added there.

81
00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.409
Let's compile and save.

82
00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:36.169
And if we have done this correctly,

83
00:03:36.169 --> 00:03:40.800
we will see this pickup interface object right here.

84
00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.479
The next thing that we need to do

85
00:03:43.479 --> 00:03:47.639
is we need to actually set up this little bit of logic

86
00:03:47.639 --> 00:03:50.939
inside of our vehicle pawn.

87
00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:54.599
And we're going to basically make this a little bit of code.

88
00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:57.680
So what we're going to do is set this up.

89
00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.759
So let's go ahead and pop back over to our editor

90
00:03:59.759 --> 00:04:01.379
really quick.

91
00:04:01.379 --> 00:04:04.099
And we are going to be doing this inside of the pawn.

92
00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:05.979
So I'm just going to come down here probably

93
00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.099
to the bottom.

94
00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:07.939
There we go.

95
00:04:07.939 --> 00:04:12.280
And we're going to look for event.

96
00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:17.379
And we want the VPI event.

97
00:04:17.379 --> 00:04:20.459
So let's just call this VPI stats.

98
00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:24.920
So we're going to look for event.

99
00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.339
And then there we go.

100
00:04:27.339 --> 00:04:29.459
Event pickup object.

101
00:04:29.459 --> 00:04:33.740
The event pickup object is what we want there.

102
00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.060
And then what we're going to do is

103
00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.939
we need to also create a new variable.

104
00:04:38.939 --> 00:04:45.180
And we're going to call this new variable current score.

105
00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.149
We're going to change it to an integer.

106
00:04:49.149 --> 00:04:49.870
integer.

107
00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.310
Let's compile and save so that we can have this current

108
00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.550
score integer ready.

109
00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:56.269
And then what we're going to do

110
00:04:56.269 --> 00:04:57.910
is we're going to pull this out.

111
00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:01.660
And we are going to get the current score.

112
00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.660
And what do we want to do with the current score?

113
00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.740
Well, we want to take the score.

114
00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.740
And we're going to go plus.

115
00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.779
I'm going to hold down shift to get a plus there.

116
00:05:09.779 --> 00:05:10.899
I said shift.

117
00:05:10.899 --> 00:05:11.819
There we go.

118
00:05:11.819 --> 00:05:12.899
And there's our ad.

119
00:05:12.899 --> 00:05:14.379
So we're going to take our score.

120
00:05:14.379 --> 00:05:17.420
And then we're going to add that to our current score.

121
00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.379
And then what we're going to do

122
00:05:18.379 --> 00:05:19.579
is we're going to take this current score.

123
00:05:19.579 --> 00:05:20.540
And we're going to drag this out.

124
00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.420
And we're going to go set.

125
00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.660
So basically, we're going to get the current score.

126
00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.740
If we score, we're going to take that current score.

127
00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.699
We're going to add to it.

128
00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:28.699
And then what we're going to do

129
00:05:28.699 --> 00:05:33.819
is we're going to set the current score to that new value.

130
00:05:33.819 --> 00:05:35.660
Now, what we're going to do next

131
00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.139
is we are going to get our time.

132
00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:40.420
But remember, our time is set in our game mode.

133
00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:44.389
So what we're going to do is we're going to get game.

134
00:05:44.389 --> 00:05:46.629
Oops, and it'd help if I would spell that right.

135
00:05:46.629 --> 00:05:49.189
So get game mode.

136
00:05:49.189 --> 00:05:49.790
There we go.

137
00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:51.550
So there's our get game mode.

138
00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.550
And then from our game mode, we

139
00:05:53.550 --> 00:06:00.949
are going to cast to advanced vehicle game mode.

140
00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.410
And we're going to actually right click on this

141
00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:06.110
and convert this to a pure cast.

142
00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.750
The reason we're doing this is it allows

143
00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:12.629
us to not have to do it in validation check

144
00:06:12.629 --> 00:06:13.870
on this particular one.

145
00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:16.629
Since we know that we are specifically

146
00:06:16.629 --> 00:06:20.269
going to this particular advanced vehicle game mode,

147
00:06:20.269 --> 00:06:22.110
and we know that the value is in there,

148
00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.670
we can use this like this without having

149
00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:26.189
to actually put in a check to see

150
00:06:26.189 --> 00:06:27.889
if this cast is going to fail.

151
00:06:27.889 --> 00:06:29.310
Then what we're going to do is

152
00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.589
we're going to pull off of this,

153
00:06:30.629 --> 00:06:34.399
and we're going to look for time.

154
00:06:34.399 --> 00:06:37.720
We are going to get our time remaining because we

155
00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.199
want to get what time is left.

156
00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:44.199
And then similarly to what we did up here,

157
00:06:44.199 --> 00:06:50.790
where we have this going out and then setting

158
00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.430
our current score, we're going to do

159
00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.670
the same thing with our time.

160
00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:54.709
So basically what we're going to do

161
00:06:54.709 --> 00:06:56.509
is we're going to take our time remaining,

162
00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:02.459
and we are going to plus add our time.

163
00:07:02.459 --> 00:07:04.699
And I'm going to flip these nodes around like this.

164
00:07:04.699 --> 00:07:05.360
So there we go.

165
00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.629
So we take our time, and then we

166
00:07:07.629 --> 00:07:09.899
add that to our time remaining.

167
00:07:09.899 --> 00:07:20.459
And then we are going to look for that time.

168
00:07:20.459 --> 00:07:23.199
And there we go, set time remaining.

169
00:07:23.199 --> 00:07:26.360
And then we're just going to connect this current score

170
00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.040
to our set time remaining.

171
00:07:28.079 --> 00:07:31.319
We're going to plug the add into the time remaining.

172
00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:33.240
And the target is actually going

173
00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.439
to be coming from our vehicle advanced game mode.

174
00:07:36.439 --> 00:07:37.959
So let's clean this up really quick

175
00:07:37.959 --> 00:07:39.800
to make it a little bit easier to read.

176
00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:43.040
So we're going to pull this down, set this up like so.

177
00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.759
One of the cool things you can do with your Blueprint

178
00:07:45.759 --> 00:07:49.120
wires to make things a little bit easier to read

179
00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:51.160
is we can double click on a wire

180
00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.720
and add what's known as a reroute.

181
00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.220
And a reroute is just going to make it a little bit easier

182
00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.560
to see where that wire is going.

183
00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.079
It doesn't add anything additional to your Blueprint.

184
00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.040
It's not going to make it run slower or faster

185
00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.040
or anything like that.

186
00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.279
It's just going to make it easier to see what's going on.

187
00:08:06.279 --> 00:08:08.199
And as you're seeing here, I like

188
00:08:08.199 --> 00:08:12.920
to put variables underneath the addition pin.

189
00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:14.800
That's just a personal preference of mine.

190
00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.519
So there we go.

191
00:08:15.519 --> 00:08:18.040
That is our final setup right here.

192
00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.120
So we have our event pickup object.

193
00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.879
And then based on that pickup object,

194
00:08:21.879 --> 00:08:24.600
whether it is going to give a score or time,

195
00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.399
we are going to either set our time, our current score, which

196
00:08:28.399 --> 00:08:30.319
is going to be inside of the vehicle pond,

197
00:08:30.319 --> 00:08:34.840
or set our time, which is inside of our game mode.

198
00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.879
So that does it for this part.

199
00:08:36.879 --> 00:08:38.980
Make sure you compile and save.

200
00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.440
And we will see you in the next part of this video

201
00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:46.279
tutorial series, setting up our score and time pickup.
